---
// Explanatory diagram: equal placed volume, different estimated order weight.
---
<section class="section deco-visual" aria-labelledby="deco-visual-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 id="deco-visual-title">The same bed takes the same volume, but a different weight</h2>
      <div class="section-divider"></div>
      <p>Choose stone for the setting first. Its loose bulk weight changes the tons on the truck, while area and finished depth determine the volume.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="deco-diagram">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 900 310" role="img" aria-labelledby="deco-svg-title deco-svg-desc">
        <title id="deco-svg-title">Decorative rock volume and weight comparison</title>
        <desc id="deco-svg-desc">A 100 square foot bed at three inches deep takes 25 cubic feet of either lava rock or marble chips. At example loose weights, that is 0.69 US tons of lava rock or 1.25 US tons of marble chips.</desc>
        <defs>
          <pattern id="deco-lava-pattern" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <rect width="25" height="25" fill="#7f3027"/><circle cx="7" cy="8" r="4" fill="#a94c3c"/><circle cx="18" cy="17" r="5" fill="#56241f"/><circle cx="21" cy="5" r="2" fill="#d77755"/>
          </pattern>
          <pattern id="deco-marble-pattern" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <rect width="25" height="25" fill="#d7dce0"/><path d="M0 20 L9 8 L19 13 L25 4" stroke="#a2abb4" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/><path d="M3 2 L13 5 M19 24 L24 19" stroke="#f9fafb" stroke-width="4"/>
          </pattern>
        </defs>
        <text x="450" y="33" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e5e7eb" font-size="19" font-weight="700">100 sq ft × 3 in finished depth = 25 ft³ (0.93 yd³)</text>
        <rect x="45" y="70" width="370" height="108" rx="14" fill="url(#deco-lava-pattern)" stroke="#c26a56" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="485" y="70" width="370" height="108" rx="14" fill="url(#deco-marble-pattern)" stroke="#f8fafc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="230" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f2f2f2" font-size="19" font-weight="700">Lava rock</text>
        <text x="670" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f2f2f2" font-size="19" font-weight="700">Marble chips</text>
        <text x="230" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#cbd5e1" font-size="16">0.75 short ton / yd³ example</text>
        <text x="670" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#cbd5e1" font-size="16">1.35 short tons / yd³ example</text>
        <text x="230" y="277" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fbbf24" font-size="26" font-weight="800">about 0.69 ton</text>
        <text x="670" y="277" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fbbf24" font-size="26" font-weight="800">about 1.25 tons</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Diagram is a quantity comparison, not a scale rendering or product photograph. Values exclude any extra material and are rounded; actual loose weight varies by product and moisture.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="deco-read">
      <div><strong>What stays fixed</strong><p>The 25 ft³ of space to fill and 50 bags if each bag really contains 0.5 ft³.</p></div>
      <div><strong>What changes</strong><p>Bulk tonnage, handling weight, local price, delivery options and sometimes the depth needed for the stone size.</p></div>
      <div><strong>What to check</strong><p>Read the bag's volume or coverage statement. For a bulk order, ask the supplier for their loose weight per cubic yard.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .deco-visual { background:var(--bg-body); }
  .deco-diagram { margin:0; background:#111a27; border:1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius:var(--radius-lg); padding:var(--space-4); }
  .deco-diagram svg { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
  .deco-diagram figcaption { color:#cbd5e1; font-size:.78rem; line-height:1.5; margin:var(--space-3) var(--space-2) 0; }
  .deco-read { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:var(--space-4); margin-top:var(--space-4); }
  .deco-read > div { padding:var(--space-4); background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius:var(--radius-md); }
  .deco-read strong { color:var(--text-primary); }
  .deco-read p { color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.86rem; line-height:1.55; margin:.4rem 0 0; }
  @media(max-width:720px) { .deco-read { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .deco-diagram { overflow-x:auto; } .deco-diagram svg { min-width:580px; } }
</style>
